{"id":"000VPQ","title":"Crop Circles","author":"pagedo","solvedCount":2,"difficulty":1,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-10-26T14:21:40+00:00","posted":"Heute, 11:19 Uhr","rules":"Normal Sudoku Rules apply.\n\nAll large circles are counting circles. Some counting circles share the circle with an arrow and/or a double arrow clue.\n\nCounting Circles: A digit on a circle indicates the number of circles containing that digit.\n\nArrows: Digits along single grey Arrow lines sum to the number in the circled cell. Digits may repeat along arrows if allowed by other rules.\n\nDouble Arrows: The sum of the digits along a double grey double arrow line is equal to the sum of the digits in the circles at either end of the line.\n\nDigits in cells joined by an X sum to 10.\n\nDigits in cells joined by a white dot are consecutive. Digits in cells joined by a black dot are in a 2:1 ratio.\n\nNot all Xs or dots are necessarily given.\n\nEnjoy your harvesting of the Circles.\n\nSolve with SudokuPad\n\n--------------------------------\n\nHope you enjoy it. Feel free to give feedback.\n\nThanks\n\n---------------------------------","solutionCode":"Row 3 digits","tags":["Sudoku","XV Pairs (Variante)","Kropki Pairs (Variante)","Arrows (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/v1vvhw9zx3","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/v1vvhw9zx3","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","arrows","overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-26T14:21:40+00:00"}